  "summary": "Tsuitate no Danjo (衝立の男女, \"Man and Woman by a Partitioning Screen\", c.",
  "description": "Tsuitate no Danjo (衝立の男女, \"Man and Woman by a Partitioning Screen\", c. 1797) is a title given to a multicolour print by the Japanese ukiyo-e artist Kitagawa Utamaro.  It depicts a young man and woman by a tsuitate partitioning screen.  The print delivers the feeling of several layers of translucency as the woman peers through the folded cloth of the man's haori and the man is seen through a silk gauze–covered portion of the tsuitate.",
